  WrittenDialogue: "I think you’ve progressed far enough.\nJust trying to get this over with, dude.\n...Is that really how you approach life?\nBasically.\nBeing forced to play my game would make anyone impatient.. {1.2}But it seems you’ve been this way for a while.\nI’m so not here to have a conversation about this.  Especially after you sicced a future mass shooter at me.\nFuture I’m not so sure about,{1} maybe an alternate one.\nAre you about to zap me to a universe somehow more misogynistic than this one?\nNo I’m talking about what could’ve been. What might’ve happened to that boy if I hadn’t shown up.\nI gave him purpose, you know. Upon finding him he was desperate and lonely, far closer to committing atrocities than he is now.\nFor how long? I can’t say. The petty hobby of serving me will only take him so far.\nHe is wearing a trench coat now. Do you know what that means?\nOf course I do! They’ll run out of pizza rolls and he’ll shoot up the frozen food aisle!\nBut isn’t it nice my puzzle is here to delay the inevitable? \nI thought it was a test of “logic and wit”?\nFor you girls it was... But my puzzle serves many purposes, for many different people.\nThe purpose of holding us digitally hostage?\nHow many times can I explain it? You already were digitally hostage! All I did was change the application.\nYeah but at least before I was... Y’know...\nHappy?{1} In control?  {1.8}We both know that’s not true.\nDude just shut up and play me so I can get this over with!\nTelling me to play... who’s truly a pawn? Get ready."
  DialogueCharacterNames: "THE PUZZLER\nNICOLE\nTHE PUZZLER\nNICOLE\nTHE PUZZLER\nNICOLE\nTHE PUZZLER\nNICOLE\nTHE PUZZLER\nTHE PUZZLER\nTHE PUZZLER\nNICOLE\nTHE PUZZLER\nTHE PUZZLER\nNICOLE\nTHE PUZZLER\nNICOLE\nTHE PUZZLER\nNICOLE\nTHE PUZZLER\nNICOLE\nTHE PUZZLER"
